# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored — your real values
# stay on your machine. Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_* is shipped to the
# client bundle, so only put non-secret defaults in there.

# A file path that the editor auto-opens on `npm run tauri dev` start. The
# path must match the OS Tauri runs on — use /mnt/c/... when running the
# Linux build inside WSL, C:\... for a native Windows build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRMPTR_DEV_FILE=/mnt/c/Users/you/Notes/scratch.md

# Optional: which view-mode to start in. One of: single | cowork | folder | history
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRMPTR_DEV_VIEW_MODE=folder
